      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:7:2:9",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّ فِي كِتَابِ عَلِيٍّ ( عليه السلام ) أَنَّ الْيَمِينَ الْكَاذِبَةَ وَ قَطِيعَةَ الرَّحِمِ تَذَرَانِ الدِّيَارَ بَلَاقِعَ مِنْ أَهْلِهَا وَ تُنْغِلُ الرَّحِمَ يَعْنِي انْقِطَاعَ النَّسْلِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Mahboub, from Malik Bin Atiyya, from Abu Ubeyda Al Haza’a, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘In the Book of Ali<sup>asws</sup> is that the false oath, and the cutting-off of relationships both devastate the houses to be deserted from its inhabitants, and locks the wombs, meaning the cutting-off of the lineage’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "9. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn Mahbub from Malik ibn ‘Atiyyah from abu ‘Ubaydah al- Hadhdha’ who has narrated the following: “Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that it is in the book of Ali, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, that false oath and cutting off of good relations with relatives leave a town barren, empty of its inhabitants and destroys the reproducing continuum.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
